      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_292e014fcf589f8ffaad16c75d1b82d0e9ccf253268245c069883f6d56c35201",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A global positive aggregate can be made tractable by decomposing it into finite data where uniform estimates are wasteful and one-sided analytic bounds for the exterior. In the Lehmer-pair calculation, nearby gaps bound a local window and separately bounded components are added before a normalized threshold test. In the zero-free-region calculations, verified low-zero data sharpen a reciprocal-square tail, and an infinite peaked-kernel integral is partitioned into compact numerical pieces and analytically bounded outer regions.",
