      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_57ae5b3b289b56cc63d45c004bf054d56e620fd416e07c26531ec28fa859ca8f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Rigorous computation should export a bounded premise, not an extrapolated global trend. A verified prefix of zeros supports RH only below its certified height; it can yield a different unconditional consequence beyond that range only when a separate theorem explicitly maps the finite threshold to that consequence, as in the upper bound for the de Bruijn-Newman constant.",
